Hi everyone,

I have prepared my openpilot fork for the Peugeot 3008 II P84 pre-facelift, roughly 2017–2020 models ( COMMA 4 - master branch based)

My own car is a 2019 Peugeot 3008, so this is the configuration I tested.

At the moment, this fork is compatible only with the Peugeot 3008 P84 pre-facelift.
For the Peugeot 5008, please contact me first. It will probably need an additional fingerprint.

If your Peugeot 3008 has Lane Centering Assist, it should work with this fork:

https://github.com/cristianku/openpilot

During the openpilot installation, when asked for a custom repo, enter:

cristianku/peugeot-3008

I also added smoothing to the steering controller to remove the small steering jerks.
This is done through a torque factor that smooths the steering torque request and makes the steering assist feel more stable and progressive.

Important safety notes:

On tight curves, if the required steering torque is too high, the steering assist may drop out / release steering support without any warning from the car or from openpilot.

Below around 54 km/h, steering assist is disabled.
The Peugeot 3008 normally enables Lane Centering Assist only above around 80 km/h, while with this openpilot fork it can work down to about 53–54 km/h.

Be careful: openpilot may still appear green / active below this speed, but the steering assist can disappear without warning at the moment.

Driving assist activation works from 30 km/h and above, as it does from factory. This cannot currently be changed.
In this case:

   
openpilot becomes green
the car’s adaptive cruise / distance control activates
longitudinal control is handled by the car, not by openpilot
openpilot starts providing steering assist only above about 54 km/h
below that speed, steering assist stops again

Thanks to @elkoled  for the initial base for this model and your past support. 
